	<td colspan=12 bgcolor="#6e6d6a" align=middle><font face="Arial,Helvetica" color=#FFFFFF size=4>Lore Keepers' Charter</font></td>
</tr>
<tr>
	<td>
		</P><P><BR><b>Mission Statement</b></P>
		<P>The primary purpose of the Lore Keepers is to gather and disseminate information about the world of 
		Norrath both through research and through action. Secondarily, we strive to help our fellow citizens of Norrath, 
		through assistance, encouragement, and example.</P>
		<P><b>Code of Conduct</b></P><P>Being a Lore Keeper is not only a privilege, but a heavy responsibility. So 
		long as a member wears the Lore Keeper tag, he or she represents ALL members of the Lore Keepers, for good and 
		for bad. Since our reputation is important in this game, we have developed a Code of Conduct which all candidates 
		must agree to before becoming full members.</P>
		<P>1. There will be no kill stealing from or intentional training onto other players. <BR>
		2. Members will abide by GM wishes at all times<BR>
		3. Members will not publically ridicule other players, nor use language in zone wide chat which some may find 
		offensive.<BR>
		4. Members will be willing to live by the Play Nice Policies instituted by Verant. This includes sharing spawn 
		sites when asked.<BR>
		5. Members are expected to follow established loot rules in any group or raid. If there are no rules, the member 
		is expected to help set rules prior to looting.<BR>
		6. A Lore Keeper is REQUIRED to give any and all officers names that are online when asked. <BR>
		7. Begging other players, either guildmates or non-guild, will not be tolerated.<BR>
		8. Lore Keepers who wish to be anonymous are urged to use /roleplay instead of /anon</P>
		<P>If you are found violating the Code, you will be warned by an officer, and all other officers shall be 
		informed of the warning. For a second offense, the member shall be put into a probationary status. A 
		punishment-decided upon by the officers-must be carried out within a set period of time to return the member 
		to good standing within the guild. A third violation will result in expulsion from the guild. Only the Guild 
		Leader may make the final decision of involuntary expulsion, although any officer can carry out the removal.</P>
		<P><b>Membership requirements</b></P><P>To become a member of the Lore Keepers, a candidate must have achieved 
		his or her twelth level. If the candidate has not reached the twelth level, the officers may vote to waive that 
		requirement. The candidate must have two sponsors, or the recommendation of an officer. Within 24 hours of being
		invited, the potential member must submit their information to the Guild Registrar via the website. Only upon 
		reciept of this information does a player become a full member of the Lore Keepers. Failure to submit information 
		will result in removal.</P><P>Secondary characters need only submit their information to the Registrar to be 
		invited. There is no level limitation for secondary characters.</P>
		<P><b>Officers</b></P><P>To help maintain the structure of the guild, there will be a High Council of Officers. 
		This will include the Guild Leader, the Tome Keepers, the Webkeeper, the Quartermaster, and the Sage. All will 
		have one vote on the Council.  However, only the Guild leader and Tome Officers will be given the privilege of 
		inviting new members.</P>
		<P><b>Guild Leader</b></P><P>The Guild Leader is the head of the guild, and its official 
		spokesperson. Only the Guild Leader has the right to appoint new officers, and to allow involuntary removals. 
		The Guild Leader is charged with upholding the Code, and for mediating disputes. The Guild Leader is also 
		responsible for establishing and maintaining interguild relationships. The Guild Leader shall be assisted by 
		the High Council.</P>
		<P><b>Tome Keepers</b></P><P>Each Class shall have a Keeper of the Tome. The primary responsibility 
		of a Tome Keeper is to research and understand how best to play his or her chosen class, and to disseminate this 
		information to others. The Tome Keepers are also responsible for mentoring others within their class.</P>
		<P><b>Webkeeper</b></P><P>The Webkeeper will be in charge of maintaining the website, and making the ultimate 
		decisions regarding the website.</P>
		<P><b>Guild Registrar</b></P><P>The Registrar shall be charged with the task of 
		maintaining a complete, comprehensive, and up to date list of all guild members, their classes, levels, and 
		alternate characters. The Registrar will also be responsible for maintaining the Class List and the Skill Master 
		list.</P>
		<P><b>Guild Quartermaster</b></P><P>The Quartermaster will be in charge of distributing items donated to the 
		guild as well as items obtained during guild raids. The decision of who shall receive the items shall be 
		ultimately the Quartermaster's, and shall only be overrulled by a majority vote of the officers. The ranking 
		system will be used by the Quartermaster to help determine item placement, but will not be the only factor, as 
		raid participation and guild assistance will also be factors. The Quartermaster may also require members to 
		complete quests to earn items.</P>
		<P><b>Guild Sage</b></P><P>The Sage will coordinate the accumulation of various words, runes, pages,and items 
		needed for spell research. There may be several mules created on many accounts, but the ultimate control over 
		these items falls to the Sage. The Sage will also have knowledge of what combinations must be used to create 
		spells.</P><P>Additionally:</P>
		<P><b>Crisis Officer</b></P><P>Each week there will be an officer assigned to assist in urgent problems, most 
		notably, organizing corpse retrievals. That officer will be available via email as well as online. The officer 
		will also be in charge of notifying the Council of those members who volunteer.</P>
		<P><b>Lore Keeper of the Month</b></P><P>The Council will elect one member of month to hold the honorary title 
		of &quot;Lore Keeper of the Month&quot;. This member will be one who has gone far above and beyond the 
		expectations of a regular member in service to the guild.   Nominations can be made at any time, by any member.</P>
		<P><b>Skill Masters</b></P><P>Any member who has reached the master level (100 skill) in a skill may elect to be 
		added to the list of Skill Masters. These members agree to assist other guild members through their skill at cost. 
		Members taking advantage of this service are responsible for the cost of failures, though. This includes-but is 
		not limited to-trade skills, research, and languages.</P>
		<P><b>Loot Rules</b></P><P>As stated in the Code, members are expect to follow loot rules as set by the group. 
		Rules set by the raid leader will supercede those of the group leader. Noncompliance with this is considered a 
		serious violation of personal and guild honor, and will result in involuntary removal.</P><P>From time to time, 
		there will be raids run by the guild. Only those raids posted in the Blackboard forum will constitute official 
		guild raids, and will be subject to guild raid rules. During an official guild raid, all items belong to the 
		guild, and shall be given to the Quartermaster for redistribution. If there is no one in the guild who can use 
		the item, the Quartermaster may make the decision to sell the item and use the proceeds to purchase other items 
		needed for the guild. Coin loot dropped during a guild raid shall be the possession of the individual who looted. 
		There will be times when raids are organized around getting a member a certain item. This must be posted in 
		advance, when the raid is posted, and that member will be given the first of the item. Any other items, as well 
		as multiples of the intended item, will be given to the Quartermaster.</P><P>Other raids consisting of Lore Keeper 
		only groups shall set their own rules amongst themselves, or by the raid leader. Items received during normal play 
		(including Lore Keeper only groups) will be owned solely by the member who wins them.</P>
		<P><b>Class List</b></P><P>There will be a ranking system in place to rank the top 5 members of each class by level. 
		If there is more than one member in a class of the same level, the member to attain the level first will be listed 
		higher. The intent of this list is to encourage friendly competition among members, thereby providing incentive for 
		them to develop and maintain their characters. It will also serve as a source for consultation for developing 
		members. No other special privilege is attached to a ladder ranking besides the recognition associated with it. 
		Attaining and maintaining a ladder ranking should not interfere with normal game play (groups, raids etc).</P>
		<P><b>Assistance</b></P><P>One of the advantages of guild membership is the assistance and support available from 
		a community of people. There is no dishonor in asking for help. Those needing help, however, should realize that 
		other people in the game want to have fun. Teleporting people around constantly, or stopping play to perform 
		resurrections can be a major problem for players with those abilities. Be prudent  when you ask for help. Requests 
		for assistance should not be repeated over and over so as to become begging. Similarly, a member asking for help 
		should be taken seriously. Help if you can, as you would want to be helped. </P><P>Common courtesy dictates that 
		requests for assistance be acknowledged in GuildChat so that they understand that help is or is not currently 
		available.  The screen clutter associated with normal game play may mean that someone misses a specific message 
		and needs to be reminded. An acknowledgement eliminates the redundancy.</P>
		<P><b>Meetings</b></P><P>To be a truly strong guild, and a close family, it is important that we meet each other 
		in &quot;person&quot;, and discuss the happenings of the guild. Therefore, we will have a full guild meeting once 
		a month. This meeting time will be posted no less than one week prior to the date of the meeting. While it is 
		understandable that real life events occur which will take precedence, meeting attendance is strongly encouraged. 
		Being online during a meeting but not in attendance at the meeting is frowned upon, and multiple occurances of this 
		may result in a review of membership. Rides will be made as available as possible, although it is the member's 
		responsibility to get to a druid ring or a wizard spire themselves. Attendance with an alternate character is 
		acceptable.</P><P>There will also be an officers' meeting no less than twice each month. The meeting time will 
		be posted in the officers section of the Forum, a week prior to the meeting. Again, attendance is vital to the 
		functioning of the guild.</P>
		<P><b>Communication</b></P><P>The primary tool of communication for the Lore Keepers will 
		be a bulletin board accessible through our website. At a minimum, the board will include a General forum open to 
		all, a Blackboard forum for raid posting, and a restricted Officers forum for Council discussion. Email is good, 
		though secondary, way of communicating between members, and all members shall make their best effort to check 
		their email on a daily basis. Email addresses of the Guild Leader, Webkeeper, and Registrar will be available to 
		the public. </P><p><p>
		The Lore Keepers would like to thank the Crimson Legacy for their assistance in 
the creation of our charter.
